  "tile_count_revision_explanations": {
    "rsvqa_tiles_5_to_9": "Why RSVQA tiles changed from 5 to 9: Early prototypes and high-level summaries only counted the 5 primary terrestrial tiles covering the inland heartland of the Netherlands (31UET, 31UFT, 31UFU, 31UGT, 31UGU). However, full national border coverage requires 9 Sentinel-2 MGRS tiles to encompass coastal borders, the Wadden Islands (31UFV, 31UGV), and eastern border fringes (32ULC, 32UMC). All 9 tiles are strictly located in the Netherlands and verified disjoint from BigEarthNet.",
    "bigearthnet_tiles_125_to_103": "Why BigEarthNet tiles changed from 125 to 103: The original optical-only BigEarthNet benchmark (Sumbul et al. 2019) cataloged 125 Sentinel-2 tiles across 10 European nations. When BigEarthNet-MM and reBEN (Clasen et al. 2024) introduced multi-modal pairing with Sentinel-1 SAR and rigorous quality control, 22 tiles were excluded due to missing S1 GRD orbits, persistent cloud contamination, or seasonal snow anomalies, leaving 103 verified dual-modal tiles."
  },
